    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d33">

                <pb facs="0032" n="24" xml:id="pg24"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">756.94/142: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-12T12:00:00+09:00">June 12,
                        1940—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received June 12—3:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>439. Our 170, March 12, 5 p.m.,<anchor n="45" xml:id="d33-f1"/> heading 3,
                    sub-division 2, Japanese enterprises in Netherlands East Indies.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>My Netherlands colleague told me last night that he yesterday invited Mr.
                        Nishi, Director of European and Western Asiatic Affairs of the Foreign
                        Office, to lunch alone with the Minister at the Legation and that in the
                        course of conversation Nishi said that the Japanese navy is pressing the
                        Foreign Office to obtain concessionary rights to explore for new oil fields
                        in the Netherlands East Indies in order to afford oil reserves for the
                        navy.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>On my telling the Minister of the categorical assurances given me by the
                        Minister for Foreign Affairs in our conversation of June 10<anchor n="46"
                            xml:id="d33-f2"/> that Japan has no territorial ambitions, General Pabst
                        said that he believed this to be entirely true so far as the Government is
                        concerned but that on the other hand Japan has economic ambitions and that
                        economic penetration is consistently dangerous.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
